---
# Reusable content component (dsl §13): a named, parameterized block of lines +
# staging expanded inline by `::use`. Presentational only — `@cue` is the sole
# ref namespace (a param), bound to the invocation arg at expansion time. Like a
# schema doc, a component file declares no scene keys, so a STANDALONE
# `lute check` reports `E-META-MISSING`; the episode validates it transitively.
component: stinger
params:
  cue: string
---

## The Stinger Beat

/* `@cue` is legal in both attr positions, for two different reasons. `label` IS
   a `string`-typed core attr (dsl Appendix A). `mood` is NOT: dsl 0.9.0 retyped
   `::music{mood}` from `string` to `{ domain: mood }`. A domain-typed attr still
   accepts a `string`-typed component PARAMETER, because the checker treats a
   domain as an id type and never type-flags a `@ref` against one — domain
   MEMBERSHIP is checked for authored literals only. So `mood=@cue` is checked
   for neither type nor membership: the `::use` arg is judged against the param's
   `string` type, and `cue` reaches `::music` unvalidated. A component body
   carries no state read/write and no logic block (§13.4). */
::music{action="change" mood=@cue}
::vfx{type="whiteOut" label=@cue transition="fade"}
@narrator: A beat of silence, then the moment lands.
